  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA compact, cool upper level low will slide by just to our east \nlate tonight and into Sunday morning. This will bring increasing\nclouds from the north and northeast, spreading down into the \nTwin Tiers by daybreak. Scattered to broken cloud cover is\nexpected for most of the forecast area Sunday morning, then\ngradually clearing by the afternoon hours as the compact low\nraces off the southern New England/Long Island coast by Sunday\nevening. There could be a few isolated showers around Sunday\nmorning, mainly for the Mohawk Valley and Catskills. Northwest\nwinds will also be breezy, between 8-15 mph, with gusts up to 25\nmph possible at times. It will certainly be cooler, and much\nless humid, but high temperatures are still expected to reach\ninto the 70s across Central NY, with mid-70s to mid-80s in NE PA.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nAfter a brief reprieve from the heat on Sunday, an upper level \nridge starts to build back in from the west by the beginning of \nthe work week. This dome of high pressure will move slowly to \nthe east into the middle of the week with afternoon high \ntemperatures rising back into the mid to upper 80s on Monday and\ninto the upper 80s and lower 90s on Tuesday through Friday. \n\nThere does appear to be some concern for a short wave breaking \nover the northern periphery of the ridge on Wednesday, which \nwould likely lead to another round of thunderstorms...potentially\nstrong to severe. This pattern repeats going into the end of \nthe week as the ridge attempts to build back in and several more\nwaves, with plenty of moisture, try to ride eastward across the\nNortheast U.S. This will be a more typical summer-type pattern \nlater in the week.",
